#: admin/settings.php:505
msgid "Display Frequency"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:506
msgid ""
"How often a viewer is asked. There are two things to decide: whether you "
"want one email per visitor or one per video, and whether skipping the form "
"counts as having been asked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:509
msgid "Once per visitor —"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:510
msgid ""
"asked a single time and then never again, on any video, whether they submit "
"or skip."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:511
msgid "Once per visitor, unless they skip —"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:512
msgid ""
"the same, except that skipping does not count, so they keep being asked on "
"the next video until they actually submit once. Then they are never asked "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:513
msgid "Once per video —"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:514
msgid ""
"asked on every video, but never twice on the same one. Skipping counts as "
"asked. Use this when each video should collect its own lead."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:515
msgid "Once per video, unless they skip —"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:516
msgid ""
"the same, except that skipping leaves that video free to ask again; only a "
"submission stops it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:517
msgid "Every time a video is played —"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:518
msgid ""
"nothing is remembered, so the form returns each time the page is loaded. "
"Expect fewer leads and more annoyance."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:522
msgid "Once per visitor"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings.php:523
